USOS 3.1.2-usos5 patch 6/6 (2026-10-13): ACPI 1.0 view for legacy systems

ACPI 1.0 operating systems (Windows 2000's ACPI HAL, XP) find the tables
only through RSDP.RsdtAddress -> RSDT and read only the 32-bit FADT fields
(FIRMWARE_CTRL, DSDT, PM1/PM2/PM_TMR/GPE blocks). CSMWrap copied the
firmware RSDP as is, and create_patched_rsdt() returned NULL when
RsdtAddress was 0, so such a firmware gave a legacy OS no ACPI tables at
all. New src/usos_acpi10.c (own code from the public ACPI specification,
no EFI dependency) runs on CSMWrap's RSDP copy before the helper-core MADT
patch: RsdtAddress 0, an invalid RSDT or one that lacks the FACP/APIC the
XSDT lists -> a new RSDT from the XSDT entries below 4 GiB; FADT 32-bit
fields 0 with the X_ field set below 4 GiB (blocks only in System I/O
space) -> a FADT copy with them filled, referenced from the RSDT only (the
XSDT keeps the firmware FADT); RsdtAddress, checksum and extended checksum
of the RSDP copy fixed. New tables live in EfiACPIReclaimMemory below
4 GiB. A valid ACPI 1.0 view is not touched. Everything is logged through
CSMWrap's printf ("USOS ACPI10: ..."; screen with verbose = true, serial
with serial = true). create_patched_rsdt() now starts from the RSDP copy.

Windows 2000 only (csmwrap.ini acpi_legacy_fadt = true, written by
tools/xp_csmwrap_esp.sh for the 2000 ACPI flow): the RSDT's FACP is always
a copy cut to the ACPI 1.0 layout (revision 1, length 116, 32-bit fields
filled). The 2000 ACPI HALs copy FADT.Length bytes into a fixed 0x84-byte
buffer; a revision 3+ FADT (0xF4+ bytes) overwrites the HAL's MADT/IOAPIC
data in HAL phase 0. The XSDT keeps the firmware FADT; XP and every other
flow see no change from this option. With the same option the DSDT and
SSDTs reached through the RSDT are copies in which every static resource
template's QWord Address Space descriptor reaching above 4 GiB is cleared
(Min/Max/Translation/Length 0, the firmware's own "unused window" form):
the 2000 acpi.sys keeps only the low 32 bits of a QWord Length and stops
with STOP 0xA5 (0x2, ...) in its PCI root window check (QEMU q35's 64-bit
window). The firmware tables and the XSDT view stay unchanged.

Applies to CSMWrap 3.1.2 (808ac8e) with its seabios submodule (578d260b)
after patches 0001-0005, patch -p1 from the top of the tree. Part of
CSMWrap 3.1.2-usos5, a MODIFIED version made by the USOS project
(LGPL-2.1 / SeaBIOS LGPLv3).

